xnu 0426: skip the shared PMR735A LDOs in the WiFi power sequence

The WiFi rail table also voted ldoe7 (PMR735A L7, the BT node's vdd-asd),
ldoc10 and ldob5. They are not in the WiFi DT supplies and their RPMh resource
can belong to another processor: measured 2026-11-25, the worker logged smpb12
and then never logged ldoe7 and never reached W1, across warm resets and with
Bluetooth off, while earlier boots had voted all eight. The RSC access wedges
rather than returning.

Keep the five PM8350/PM8350C SMPS, which are the WiFi rails, and leave the
shared LDOs to the bootloader. If the link fails without them, the next step is
an owner-safe vote through the AOP, not another direct TCS write.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index 49bfada..1a032c9 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -275,9 +275,14 @@ static const struct wifi_rail wifi_rails[] = {
 	{ "smpb10", 1800 },
 	{ "smpc1", 1900 },
 	{ "smpb12", 1350 },
-	{ "ldoe7", 2800 },
-	{ "ldoc10", 1200 },
-	{ "ldob5", 880 },
+	/*
+	 * ldoe7 is the PMR735A L7 that the BT node calls vdd-asd; ldoc10 and ldob5
+	 * are shared LDOs too. They are not in the WiFi DT supplies. Measured
+	 * 2026-11-25: after smpb12 the worker never logged ldoe7 and never reached
+	 * W1, across warm resets and with Bluetooth off; earlier boots had voted
+	 * them, so the RSC resource is contended or owned elsewhere. The five SMPS
+	 * above are the WiFi rails; the loader leaves the LDOs on.
+	 */
 };
 
 static vm_offset_t wifi_gcc, wifi_parf, wifi_phy, wifi_dbi, wifi_elbi,
